# Project
- Pure native Android app (Android only): Kotlin + Jetpack Compose, single Gradle module :app under android-native/. No React Native / Node / Metro involved.
- Stack versions (see gradle/libs.versions.toml): Gradle 8.9 wrapper, AGP 8.7.2, Kotlin 2.0.21 (+ kotlin.compose plugin), KSP 2.0.21-1.0.28, Java/JVM target 17, compileSdk/targetSdk 35, minSdk 26, Compose BOM 2024.11.00 (~1.7.x foundation/material3). Room 2.6.1 via KSP, Navigation Compose 2.8.4, DataStore Preferences 1.1.1, Lifecycle 2.8.7, coroutines 1.9.0.
- All source lives in android-native/app/src/main/java/app/pillshere/ (ui/, data/db/). DI is a hand-written AppContainer.kt — no Hilt/Koin; register new dependencies/migrations there.
- Room: schema JSON exports to android-native/app/schemas/. On any DB change, bump the version and add MIGRATION_n_m in PillshereDb, then register it in AppContainer.

# Environment
- Windows, PowerShell only (no bash, no export, no &&; chain with ;).
- Always quote paths containing spaces. Use backslashes in shell commands.
- Run Gradle through the wrapper from android-native\ : .\gradlew.bat --no-daemon <task>.

# Commands
- Build debug APK: cd android-native; .\gradlew.bat assembleDebug
- Fast compile check: cd android-native; .\gradlew.bat compileDebugKotlin
- Clean: cd android-native; .\gradlew.bat clean
- Lint: cd android-native; .\gradlew.bat lint
- Unit tests: cd android-native; .\gradlew.bat testDebugUnitTest

# Rules
- Do not change AGP, Gradle, Kotlin, KSP, JDK, or Compose BOM versions without asking first.
- Do not add or upgrade dependencies without asking; when approved, declare them in gradle/libs.versions.toml — never hardcode versions in build.gradle.kts files.
- Do not edit generated or build folders (android-native/app/build, android-native/.gradle, ksp-generated code under app/build/generated/).
- Keep changes small and scoped to the task. No unrelated refactors.
- When debugging a build error, read the full error output first, change one thing at a time, and do not retry a fix that already failed. If an artifact looks corrupt, inspect it inside C:\Users\<user>\.gradle\caches\modules-2 before deleting any cache directory (deletion is destructive → ask first).
- After changes, run the build or lint command and report the actual result, including failures.
- Ask before deleting files or running anything destructive.
